[[File:E 004.png|thumb|[[Pigge|Pigge]], the first example of a Red enemy]]
'''Red Enemies''' (Japanese: 赤い敵 ''Akai Teki'') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] and the first trait introduced, appearing as early as [[Maldives (Empire of Cats)|Maldives/Tokushima]]. Red enemy variants are usually more powerful than their existing counterparts and have greater durability, getting knocked back less and in some cases can push aggresively. Reds are usually either extremely fast or slow. Most Red enemies also have a fairly high money drop, and tend to be stat-based, lacking reliance on [[Special Abilities|special abilities]].

See [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Red abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Waterblast Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Red enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Red enemies are associated with Red [[Catfruit]], which can be obtained from the [[Growing Catfruit]] stage [[Red Passions]].
*Anti-Red abilities are improved by the [[Blood Fruit]] from [[Into the Future]].
*Red [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Red|Red Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Red|Red Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Red|Red Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Crimson Dawn]], [[Crimson Apex]], [[Crimson Refuge]]
**[[Baron Seal Strikes]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Baron Seal Strikes/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Baron Seal Strikes/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Baron Seal Strikes/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*In [[Nyanko Defence Force]], [[Jackie Peng]] had Red, [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variants that have not appeared in other games.
**Nyanko Defence Force also had a standalone Red variant of [[Doge]], which only existed in the form of [[Lord Enma]]'s rider until [[Kaijin Doge]] was added.
*According to their Japanese descriptions, [[Sir Seal]] dyed himself Red after coming to Tokyo, while the [[Cerberus Kids]] were Red until they came to Tokyo.
*[[Rain D.]] hates Red. Don't ask why.

